### 1. Create a video story

POST {{baseUrl}}/story/create HTTP/1.1
Authorization: {{user}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": "Check out this video story!",
  "storyType": "VIDEO"
}

### 2. Create an image story

POST {{baseUrl}}/story/create HTTP/1.1
Authorization: {{user}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": "Beautiful sunny day out here!",
  "fileUrl": "https://storage.googleapis.com/example/stories/sample_image.jpg",
  "storyType": "IMAGE"
}

### 3. Create a text story

POST {{baseUrl}}/story/create HTTP/1.1
Authorization: {{user}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": "Excited to share this moment with everyone!",
  "storyType": "TEXT"
}

### 4. Update a story

PUT {{baseUrl}}/story/update HTTP/1.1
Authorization: {{user}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "storyId": "6aa77788f5aa48736c3c562e",
  "content": "Updated caption with new video",
  "storyType": "VIDEO"
}

### 5. Update a story (content only)

PUT {{baseUrl}}/story/update HTTP/1.1
Authorization: {{user}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "storyId": "6650a1b2c3d4e5f6a7b8c9d0",
  "content": "Updated text caption for the story"
}

### 6. Get available stories for user

GET {{baseUrl}}/story/available HTTP/1.1
Authorization: {{user}}

### 7. Get user-wise stories (returns storyType: VIDEO | IMAGE | TEXT)

# /:id -> user ID (story poster ID)

GET {{baseUrl}}/story/user/6a76854f7acbc5fdbb402ed2 HTTP/1.1
Authorization: {{user}}

### 8. Like or unlike a story

# /:id -> story ID

PATCH {{baseUrl}}/story/like-unlike/6650a1b2c3d4e5f6a7b8c9d0 HTTP/1.1
Authorization: {{user}}

### 9. Delete a story

# /:id -> story ID

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/story/delete/6650a1b2c3d4e5f6a7b8c9d0 HTTP/1.1
Authorization: {{user}}
